-- title:
--   Exchanging j(q^e) and j(q^{ep}) determines wₚ
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a nonzero natural number with $p \nmid M$ and $M \ge 5$. Write $F$ for [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L182), the subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$ generated over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ by the image, under the coefficientwise map [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) induced by $\mathbb Q \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$, of the rational function field [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldC ℚ (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L134) inside $\mathbb Q((q))$. Let $\tau$ be an $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-algebra automorphism of $F$ subject to the following exchange condition: for every nonzero $e \mid M$, any element of $F$ whose underlying Laurent series is the image under `coeffEmb` of `qExpand ℚ e jq` (the series $j$, namely $q^{-1}$ times a power series with rational coefficients, with $q$ replaced by $q^{e}$) is sent by $\tau$ to an element with underlying series the image of `qExpand ℚ (e * p) jq`, and conversely any element with underlying series the image of `qExpand ℚ (e * p) jq` is sent to one with underlying series the image of `qExpand ℚ e jq`. The conclusion is: for every $f$ in [`ModularCurve.modularFunctionFieldFull (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L305), the subfield of $\mathbb Q((q))$ generated over $\mathbb Q$ by the series `qExpand ℚ d jq` for the nonzero divisors $d$ of $M p$, and for every proof that the image of $f$ under `coeffEmb` lies in $F$, applying $\tau$ to the resulting element of $F$ yields the image under `coeffEmb` of the Laurent series of [`ModularCurve.atkinLehnerInvolutionFull M p f`](def/ModularCurve_AtkinLehnerPartial.html#L21), where the latter is the chosen $\mathbb Q$-algebra automorphism of `modularFunctionFieldFull (M * p)` interchanging `qExpand ℚ d jq` and `qExpand ℚ (d * p) jq` for all nonzero $d \mid M$ (such an automorphism existing here by [`ModularCurve.exists_isAtkinLehnerAutFull_of_prime_of_not_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_isAtkinLehnerAutFull_of_prime_of_not_dvd)).
--
--   This identifies an automorphism of $\overline{\mathbb Q}\cdot\mathbb Q(X_1(Mp))$ satisfying the exchange law $j(q^{e}) \leftrightarrow j(q^{ep})$ with the Atkin–Lehner involution $w_p$ on the subfield generated by the $j(q^{d})$, $d \mid Mp$, i.e. on $\overline{\mathbb Q}\cdot\mathbb Q(X_0(Mp))$, the point being that both maps are algebra maps agreeing on these generators. It is used in the construction of automorphisms of the function field of $X_1(Mp)$ relating the Hecke and diamond operators at $p$ to the Atkin–Lehner involution.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XOneP_coe_apply_coeffEmb_eq_coeffEmb_atkinLehnerInvolutionFull_of_atkinLehnerSlash_p.lean

